{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s patch graph and SwiftUI are both reactive dataflow. Swami targets SwiftUI’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"state graph (computed properties, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withAnimation"},{"type":"text","text":") rather than imperative"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"functions, so the two graphs stay aligned. Where a native SwiftUI construct maps"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"cleanly, Swami uses it. Where Origami’s semantics need a helper — for example the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Interaction patch’s four discrete output ports, or Drag’s momentum + rubber-band"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"physics — Swami ships a helper named after the Origami patch and shaped like it."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Swami"}],"role":"collection","title":"Swami","roleHeading":"Framework","externalID":"Swami","symbolKind":"module"},"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An Origami → SwiftUI translator: a deterministic parser reads Facebook’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".origami"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"patch graph into a semantic IR, and a codegen writes that IR out as SwiftUI. Swami"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is also the patch-matched helper library that fills gaps between Origami patches"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and native SwiftUI — one helper per Origami patch, named after the patch, sized by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s patch surface. Every pattern that lands is a deliverable, verified against"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s own render, and shipped as a DocC-embedded example."}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"topicSections":[{"anchor":"Reference","title":"Reference","identifiers":["doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/OrigamiMappings","doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Beats"]},{"anchor":"Helpers","title":"Helpers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction","doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Drag"]},{"anchor":"Examples","title":"Examples","identifiers":["doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/TouchOrigamiExampleView"]},{"generated":true,"anchor":"Extended-Modules","title":"Extended Modules","identifiers":["doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/SwiftUICore"]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swami"]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami"},"sections":[],"references":{"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/SwiftUICore":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/SwiftUICore","role":"collection","title":"SwiftUICore","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/swami\/swiftuicore","abstract":[],"type":"topic"},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/OrigamiMappings":{"kind":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/OrigamiMappings","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"How Swami translates the four kinds of Origami patch into SwiftUI’s state graph."}],"title":"Origami → SwiftUI mappings","url":"\/documentation\/swami\/origamimappings","role":"article"},"doc://samatwork.Swami/documentation/Swami/Interaction":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Interaction","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/swami\/interaction","kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"SwiftUI equivalent of Origami’s "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Interaction","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" patch."}],"type":"topic","fragments"